  "goodToKnow": "Die Wellenlänge is wavelength in physics: die Wellenlänge des Lichts. Figuratively, auf einer (or derselben) Wellenlänge liegen means to be on the same wavelength. German physicist Heinrich Hertz proved the existence of electromagnetic waves in 1886–88 in Karlsruhe, and the unit Hertz is named after him. Die Welle is a wave: die La-Ola-Welle in stadiums. Plural: die Wellenlängen."
